Ken: "In general, I have found Orlanski BCs to work better than anything else I tested, so I do recommend it. 
Basically, it appears to do a decent job in preventing spurious along-boundary pressure gradients 
(set up by a mismatch between the rest of the flow and the boundary condition).

In addition to Orlanski, you can choose to set OBCSbalance to be true as I have below (in this case,
 OBCS_balanceFacE=-1.0000e+00, OBCS_balanceFacW=1.0000e+00  means that the integrated inflow from EBC
is nudged uniformly to the integrated outflow from WBC)."




# ***************
# Open boundaries
# ***************
 &OBCS_PARM01
 useOBCSprescribe=.TRUE.,
 useOBCSsponge=.TRUE.,
 OB_Ieast  =  600*-1,
 OBEtFile='EBCt.bin',
 OBEsFile='EBCs.bin',
 OBEuFile='EBCu.bin',
 OBEvFile='EBCv.bin',
 OB_Jnorth = 510*-1,
# OBNtFile='NBCt.bin',
# OBNsFile='NBCs.bin',
# OBNuFile='NBCu.bin',
# OBNvFile='NBCv.bin',
 OB_Iwest = 600*1,
 OBWtFile='WBCt.bin',
 OBWsFile='WBCs.bin’,
 OBWuFile='WBCu.bin',
 OBWvFile='WBCv.bin',
 OB_Jsouth = 510*1,
# OBStFile='SBCt.bin',
# OBSsFile='SBCs.bin',
# OBSuFile='SBCu.bin',
# OBSvFile='SBCv.bin',
 useOrlanskiNorth=.FALSE.,
 useOrlanskiEast=.TRUE.,
 useOrlanskiSouth=.FALSE.,
 useOrlanskiWest=.TRUE.,
 useOBCSbalance=.TRUE.,
# OBCS_balanceFacN=0.0000e+00,
 OBCS_balanceFacE=-1.0000e+00,
# OBCS_balanceFacS=0.0000e+00,
 OBCS_balanceFacW=1.0000e+00,

 &
# Orlanski parameters
 &OBCS_PARM02
 cvelTimeScale=9.5600e+02,
 CMAX=4.5000e-01,
 &

# sponge layer
 &OBCS_PARM03
 spongeThickness=20,
 Urelaxobcsbound=2160.
 Urelaxobcsinner=4320000.,
 Vrelaxobcsbound=2160.
 Vrelaxobcsinner=4320000.,
 &
